  "notes": [
    {
      "topic": "admission",
      "text": "Area of Interest and other CEAS students (excluding double major applicants) are admitted if they have completed at least 10 credits of mathematics, physics, chemistry, and engineering courses (excluding EST 392, ESE 301 and CME 233) required for the major, earned a GPA of 3.2 in those courses with no more than one grade less than B-, have not repeated any required course, and have completed course evaluations for transferred courses used for the major. Applications are due January 5 (Spring) and June 5 (Fall) and must be made no later than one year after enrolling in the first course that applies toward the major. Non-CEAS students and double major applicants follow a separate, competitive process; fulfilling the requirements does not guarantee acceptance."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "The Accelerated BE/MS Degree Program in Civil Engineering is not described here; see the department website or contact the department."
    },
    {
      "topic": "sbc",
      "text": "One SBC must fulfill two objectives. CIV 440 and CIV 441 partially satisfy ESI, CER, SPK, WRTD, SBS+, STEM+, and EXP+; see the CEAS Undergraduate Student Office. The per-course SBC table was not transcribed as program rules."
    },
    {
      "topic": "advising",
